add([(1747,'statement','Classical assumptions and adaptation claims.','conflict'),(1752,'figure','Nominal-data pretraining followed by real-data refinement.','premise')],'adaptation','Conditional learning and adaptation','A pretrained dynamics network encounters an unseen payload. Which conclusion is supported without assuming an adaptation mechanism or new data?', [('It may incur model error; adaptation requires suitable data, training or an explicitly designed update mechanism.','Learning capability does not automatically update fixed weights when payload changes.'),('Its unchanged weights identify the new payload merely because its hidden layers are nonlinear.','Nonlinearity alone supplies no new parameter information.'),('Its nominal training loss measures its exact error under the new payload.','A training-domain score does not measure an unseen operating condition.'),('Keeping the old payload in the analytical label generator makes the new real payload irrelevant.','Incorrect synthetic labels can preserve the old-model mismatch.')],typ='scenario',conflict='The introduction broadly says AI models can adapt to unknown payloads without stating a data/update mechanism.')
