add([(1755,'equation','M11 cross coefficient printed 2m1l1l2cos(q2).','conflict'),(1758,'code','M11 code cross coefficient2*m2*L1*L2*cos(q2).','premise')],'mass-typo','Mass cross-term discrepancy','The equation slide uses m1 in the M11 cross term, while the code uses m2. For the illustrated tip-mass geometry, which qualification is correct?', [('The distal mass m2 supplies the coupling term; equal source masses hide the equation-slide typo.','The distal mass velocity contains both link contributions, so its kinetic-energy cross term is proportional to m2.'),('The proximal mass m1 supplies the cross term because it is nearer the base.','The proximal tip mass has no motion contribution from link 2.'),('Both expressions must disagree numerically even when m1=m2.','Equal masses make the two coefficients identical in this example.'),('Changing the mass coefficient can be compensated solely by renaming q1 as q2.','That does not preserve the stated geometry or general dynamics.')],difficulty='medium',forms=[FM,FK],steps=['The distal tip velocity includes contributions from both link rotations.','Its squared speed produces the l1l2 cos(q2) coupling multiplied by m2.','For m1=m2 the typographic substitution is numerically invisible.'],conflict='The M11 equation prints2m1l1l2cos(q2), whereas the depicted point-tip-mass model and code require2m2l1l2cos(q2).')
