add([(1769,'code','New torch.randperm per epoch and 500-epoch training loop.')],'epoch-updates','Which examples are dropped','Under the printed full 500-epoch loop, what follows from a fresh permutation each epoch and 35 batches per epoch?', [('17,500 optimizer steps; the omitted 20 rows can change identity between epochs.','The loop has 500×35 updates, and the permutation changes which indices lie in the omitted tail.'),('17,500 optimizer steps; exactly the same 20 rows are always omitted.','A new permutation does not keep a fixed tail.'),('500 optimizer steps; all minibatches share a single update at epoch end.','optimizer.step is inside the minibatch loop.'),('18,000 optimizer steps; each epoch includes a 36th partial batch.','The floor-divided loop contains only 35 batches.')],typ='code',difficulty='medium',steps=['Multiply 500 epochs by 35 batch steps.','Read randperm inside the epoch loop; the omitted tail is not a fixed dataset subset.'],assumptions=['The loop completes all 500 epochs without interruption.'])
